---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const faq = [
  {
    q: "What is PRAANA?",
    a: "An open-source terminal coding agent. It reads and edits code in your project, runs commands and tests, and works with the model provider you choose. MIT licensed, and it runs on your machine.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which providers does it work with?",
    a: "Anthropic, OpenAI, DeepSeek, Groq, Google, Mistral, xAI, Fireworks, Together, Cerebras, NVIDIA, Poolside, Umans, OpenCode, OpenRouter, Amazon Bedrock, GitHub Copilot and OpenAI Codex (OAuth sign-in), and Ollama for fully local use. PRAANA auto-detects your provider API key from the environment.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I install?",
    a: "No Bun: Linux/macOS — curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/amitkumardubey/praana/main/install.sh | bash. Windows (PowerShell) — irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/amitkumardubey/praana/main/install.ps1 | iex. With Bun: bun add -g praana or bunx praana.",
  },
  {
    q: "What do I need to run it?",
    a: "An API key for any supported provider, or a local Ollama install. The curl and PowerShell installers do not require Bun. bun add -g and bunx need Bun 1.4 or newer (bun.sh/install).",
  },
  {
    q: "Is it free and open source?",
    a: "Yes. MIT licensed, with the source on GitHub and the package on npm. The code is open to read and fork; external pull requests are not accepted.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does my code leave my machine?",
    a: "Your prompts and the tool output the model needs go to the model provider you choose. Sessions and logs are stored under ~/.praana. PRAANA also checks the npm registry for new versions (set PRAANA_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1 to turn that off) and downloads an embedding model once from Hugging Face, after you consent. With Ollama as the provider, prompts stay on your machine too.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is it better than other coding agents?",
    a: "We have not measured that, so we make no claim. PRAANA manages what the model sees on each turn, but there is no published comparison against other agents yet. A per-session telemetry scorecard exists, and a fixed evaluation suite is still to come.",
  },
];

const faqStructuredData = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faq.map(({ q, a }) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: a },
  })),
};
---

<Layout title="PRAANA" current="home">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>PRAANA</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A terminal coding agent. Open source, runs on your machine, and works with
      the model provider you already use.
    </p>
    <div class="install-block">
      <pre><code># Linux / macOS
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/amitkumardubey/praana/main/install.sh | bash

# Windows (PowerShell)
irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/amitkumardubey/praana/main/install.ps1 | iex</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="install-block">
      <span class="install-or">or with Bun</span>
      <pre><code>bun add -g praana</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p class="prereq">Installers: no Bun needed. <code>bun add -g</code>: <a href="https://bun.sh/install">Bun ≥ 1.4</a></p>
  </section>

  <div class="prose">

    <h2>Why use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Bring your own model.</strong> 18 providers, including Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, DeepSeek, Groq, OpenRouter and Amazon Bedrock, or run fully local with Ollama. Switch models mid-session with <code>/model</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Asks before risky actions.</strong> <code>rm</code>, force-push, package installs and writes outside your project need your OK. <code>/plan on</code> blocks every file change until you approve the plan.</li>
      <li><strong>Redacts secrets from tool output.</strong> Known key and token patterns are masked in tool results and in the logged tool calls.</li>
      <li><strong>Works with what you already have.</strong> Reads your <code>AGENTS.md</code> or <code>CLAUDE.md</code>, and loads <code>SKILL.md</code> skills from <code>.agents/skills</code>, <code>.cursor/skills</code> and <code>~/.claude/skills</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Real code tools.</strong> Native code search, symbol lookup, structured git, a test runner, and optional language-server diagnostics.</li>
      <li><strong>Scriptable.</strong> <code>praana run "fix the failing tests"</code> runs one task without a terminal UI, for CI and scripts.</li>
      <li><strong>Your code goes only to your model provider.</strong> Sessions and logs stay under <code>~/.praana</code>. MIT licensed.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Get started</h2>
    <pre><code>export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."   # or OPENAI_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, ...
praana</code></pre>
    <p>
      On first run without a config file, <code>praana</code> opens a short setup wizard.
      Update later with <code>praana upgrade</code>. Every install option, command and
      setting is on the <a href={`${base}reference/`}>Reference</a> page.
    </p>

    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p>
      Experimental. PRAANA manages what the model sees on each turn, but we have not
      measured whether that beats a plain transcript agent, so we don't claim it does.
      Most of the code was written by coding agents under human direction and review.
      Read the <a href={`${base}reference/`}>known limitations</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Documentation</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <a class="card" href={`${base}reference/`}>
        <strong>Reference</strong>
        <span>Install options, commands, providers, limitations</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href={`${base}architecture/`}>
        <strong>Architecture</strong>
        <span>How context and memory are built</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href={`${base}concepts/`}>
        <strong>Concepts</strong>
        <span>Glossary and mental model</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="https://github.com/amitkumardubey/praana/blob/main/ROADMAP.md">
        <strong>Roadmap</strong>
        <span>Where it is heading</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="https://github.com/amitkumardubey/praana/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">
        <strong>Feedback</strong>
        <span>Report a bug or share an idea</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2>Community</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/amitkumardubey/praana/discussions">GitHub Discussions</a> — Q&amp;A and ideas</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/amitkumardubey/praana/issues">Issues</a> — bug reports and feature requests</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/praana">npm</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>
    {faq.map(({ q, a }) => (
      <>
        <h3>{q}</h3>
        <p>{a}</p>
      </>
    ))}

  </div>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqStructuredData)} />
</Layout>
